# S8-0 (PROBE, first): the PRODUCTION profile c2-packed-tp4 on the new image, the eight-seat flag OFF (QWEN_FAST_M3_BLOCKS unset). Status of the
# four-card set, the platform serving container taken down (unserve), an all-four reset with the heal, then a smoke.
# PRODUCTION IS LIVE ON THE CARDS when this window opens. Before this job the placement is removed through the admin API (the user's go-ahead
# and an admin token; until then the node agent reloads the container within minutes); then unserve stops and removes the serving container here,
# and the reset follows, so no serving process holds a card. This is the ONLY job that takes production down; the handback job (the last one)
# puts today's production recipe back.
# What it proves: the new image does not change the production profile. c2-packed-tp4 is audits OFF with the pinned sampler recorded in the
# verify trace and the tail caps on, and the seat flag is not in it, so every path is the single-block one. The tests are concurrent4_code_equal (the
# exactness reference S8-1 is held against: flag OFF here, flag ON there, the same four prompts) and the four-user hang factorial shapes
# (concurrent4_steady, steady_resend, replay_concurrent4: the deterministic audits-off hang shapes, which an engine build after many packed rounds
# and a rows=2 sequential replay trigger).
# READ: the status listing (four boards, one firmware bundle, enough free hugepages, the serving container then gone, no holders after unserve);
# '[PINDIAG] packed-any admission passed:' and no UNQUALIFIED line; NO 'blocks=2' marker anywhere in the container log; no late prefill program;
# c2_smoke_check clean; no watchdog, stall-watch or replay-deadline exit; every concurrent user at 800 tokens; the content and reasoning hashes of
# concurrent4_code_equal EQUAL to the production smokes of the earlier windows (tp4-serve-7's B7, tp4-next-2's N0): any difference is this image and
# STOPS the window (the handback still runs).
# Duration (estimate): status 1-2 min; unserve 1-2 min; reset 3-6 min; the smoke 25-45 min: 45 / 60 / 75 min. Stop rule: any difference, refusal or
# hang stops the window.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4-seats8 window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/seats8 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN.
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. Every value is final except the image tag.
# ORDER.txt says the order, each job's image, its stop rule and its minutes. C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-seats8 is the tag the image build of this branch
# gets; no job here builds (the image is built by a build-only job while production still serves). A commit after that build needs a new
# build and a new tag in every template.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=status unserve reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-seats8
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent4_steady,steady_resend,replay_concurrent4,concurrent4_code_equal
